      "raw": "## Setting up\n\n$f$ is a product of six linear factors:\n$$f(x) = (6x+2)(-6x-1)(-3x)(-4x-3)(-5x+6)(9x+7).$$\n\nThe logarithmic-derivative form is convenient:\n$$\\frac{f'(x)}{f(x)} = \\sum_i \\frac{a_i}{L_i(x)}, \\qquad L_i(x) = a_ix+b_i.$$\n\n## Step 1: Evaluate each factor at $x=-1$\n\n- $(6(-1)+2) = -4$\n- $(-6(-1)-1) = 5$\n- $(-3(-1)) = 3$\n- $(-4(-1)-3) = 1$\n- $(-5(-1)+6) = 11$\n- $(9(-1)+7) = -2$\n\nProduct:\n$$f(-1) = (-4)(5)(3)(1)(11)(-2) = 1320.$$\n\n## Step 2: Evaluate the logarithmic sum\n\nCoefficients $a_i$: $6,\\ -6,\\ -3,\\ -4,\\ -5,\\ 9$.\n\n$$\\sum \\frac{a_i}{L_i(-1)} = \\frac{6}{-4} + \\frac{-6}{5} + \\frac{-3}{3} + \\frac{-4}{1} + \\frac{-5}{11} + \\frac{9}{-2}$$\n\n$$= -\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{6}{5} - 1 - 4 - \\frac{5}{11} - \\frac{9}{2}.$$\n\nCombine: $-\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{9}{2} = -6$, and $-6 - 1 - 4 = -11$. So\n\n$$-11 - \\frac{6}{5} - \\frac{5}{11} = -\\frac{605}{55} - \\frac{66}{55} - \\frac{25}{55} = -\\frac{696}{55}.$$\n\n## Step 3: Multiply\n\n$$f'(-1) = f(-1)\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{696}{55}\\right) = 1320 \\cdot \\left(-\\frac{696}{55}\\right) = 24 \\cdot (-696) = -16704.$$\n\n**Check (direct term-by-term):** each term is $f(-1)/L_i \\cdot a_i$:\n$-330\\cdot6 = -1980$, $264\\cdot(-6) = -1584$, $440\\cdot(-3) = -1320$, $1320\\cdot(-4) = -5280$, $120\\cdot(-5) = -600$, $-660\\cdot 9 = -5940$. Sum $= -16704$. ✓\n\n{\"answer\": \"-16704\"}",
